"""NearCrew pre-release product and policy pages; preserve actual capability limits."""
STYLE = """<style>
.fl{background:#f7f9ff;color:#172138;border-radius:22px;padding:clamp(22px,5vw,60px);margin:24px 0}.fl h1,.fl h2,.fl h3,.fl p,.fl li{color:#172138}.fl h1{font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,64px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.035em}.fl h2{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:36px}.fl p,.fl li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.65}.fl .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr .75fr;gap:36px;align-items:center}.fl .network{width:112px;height:112px;border-radius:24px}.fl .screen{width:100%;max-width:280px;height:auto;border:1px solid #ccd4ea;border-radius:18px}.fl figure{margin:0;text-align:center}.fl figcaption,.fl .small{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#52627a}.fl a{color:#244f9d}.fl .links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:24px 0}.fl .links a{padding:12px 18px;border:1px solid #2e61b8;border-radius:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700}.fl .links a.primary{background:#244f9d;color:#fff}.fl .features,.fl .gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:30px 0}.fl .features h2{font-size:21px}.fl .notice{padding:22px;border:1px solid #ccd4ea;border-radius:14px;background:#edf3fc}.fl .notice h2{margin-top:0}.fl a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #3184f6;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:720px){.fl .hero,.fl .features,.fl .gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fl .screen{max-width:250px}}
</style>"""
LINKS='<div class="links"><a href="/nearcrew/">Overview</a><a href="/nearcrew/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="/nearcrew/support/">Support</a><a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">Email support</a></div>'
def build(page):
 image='https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/nearcrew/icon.png'
 page('/nearcrew/','NearCrew Offline Chat — Nearby Group Messaging','Nearby adult group chat over Bluetooth or a local Wi-Fi hotspot. Development preview; planned $0.99 once, no ads or subscription.',STYLE+'''<article class="fl"><div class="hero"><div><p class="small">FAMILYLINK OFFLINE CHAT · ANDROID · IN DEVELOPMENT</p><img class="network" src="/assets/apps/nearcrew/icon.png" width="112" height="112" alt="NearCrew group chat icon"><h1>Stay in touch.<br>Stay nearby.</h1><p>A small group chat for the people with you. One Android phone hosts a room; nearby adults join over Bluetooth or a local Wi-Fi hotspot, with host approval.</p><p>Built for camping trips, festivals and everyday time together when you want a local connection without another account or a mobile data plan.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="#features">Explore the features</a><a href="/nearcrew/support/">Setup &amp; help</a></div><p class="small">Planned $0.99 US one-time purchase. No ads, subscription or in-app purchases. Not yet available on Google Play.</p></div><figure><img class="screen" src="/assets/apps/nearcrew/home.png" width="1080" height="2400" alt="NearCrew development app home screen"><figcaption>Actual development build. Sample profiles are used in screenshots.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="features" id="features"><section><h2>A nearby room</h2><p>One host and up to five guests. Join with a PIN or room invitation and wait for the host to approve you. The host can remove participants.</p></section><section><h2>More than a message</h2><p>Native-app chat includes text, small photos, editable own messages, short voice notes and local voice-call controls. Delivery labels distinguish local messages from messages received by the host.</p></section><section><h2>Choose your view</h2><p>Pick a profile color, switch between light and dark themes, adjust chat text size or use Simple mode with larger controls. A short tutorial explains joining.</p></section></div>
<h2>Useful tools for the group.</h2><ul><li><strong>Browser guests:</strong> a Wi-Fi host can offer a two-step invitation: join Wi-Fi, then open the chat webpage. Guests enter a name and wait for approval. Browser chat supports text and meeting acknowledgments, not native photos, voice or timed locations.</li><li><strong>A meeting plan:</strong> the host can pin a meeting place, details, time and an optional photo. Members can acknowledge the current plan.</li><li><strong>Optional locations:</strong> preview and send a location once, or explicitly start 30- or 60-minute updates for approved native-app members. Timed updates run about every five minutes and can continue with the screen locked. Stop in the app or notification. No silent tracking or movement history is provided.</li><li><strong>Group tools:</strong> send an alert to this room and see acknowledgments, or use a Morse screen, flashlight or beep signal. These tools do not contact emergency services.</li><li><strong>Local history:</strong> an encrypted, bounded recent conversation and reconnection information stay on each phone. Reopen an approved room when available, or delete saved data while disconnected.</li><li><strong>Connection checking:</strong> native Wi-Fi members can compare seven security symbols in person for their current host connection. Reconnects require a fresh comparison.</li><li><strong>Sharing and feedback:</strong> share a standalone installer where supported, or compose feedback with an optional, previewable diagnostic summary. Nothing is emailed automatically.</li></ul>
<section class="gallery"><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/nearcrew/chat.png" width="1080" height="2400" alt="NearCrew sample chat"><figcaption>Compact chat and clear delivery labels.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/nearcrew/settings.png" width="1080" height="2400" alt="NearCrew settings and support controls"><figcaption>Appearance, help and privacy.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/nearcrew/dark-home.png" width="1080" height="2400" alt="NearCrew dark theme"><figcaption>A light or dark view, your choice.</figcaption></figure></section>
<aside class="notice"><h2>A preview, with clear limits.</h2><p>NearCrew is being prepared for adults aged 18 and older: nearby friends, travel groups and campers. The app and browser ask for a local adult self-declaration, not verified identity. Social-app safety and privacy review remain part of release preparation. Two-device radio, call and timed-location testing remains part of release qualification. Screens and automated tests alone do not prove every feature works on every phone.</p><p>Everyone must remain within reach of the host. It is not a mesh network, internet messenger, remote location tracker or emergency-response service. Range, background restrictions, phone settings and interference affect delivery.</p></aside>
<h2>Private choices, explained plainly.</h2><p>No NearCrew cloud account, advertising or analytics SDK is used. Native Wi-Fi connections use TLS and saved chat uses Android Keystore-backed encryption. The host relays and can read the room’s content; this is not end-to-end group encryption.</p><p>Optional browser chat uses local HTTP. Someone able to monitor or alter that network can read or change browser traffic. Prefer the native app for sensitive conversations. Saved history has limits: 80 entries, 10 photos, 10 voice notes and 10 queued messages. Starting or joining another room replaces the saved conversation.</p><p class="small">NearCrew Offline Chat is an independent TripperDeeLabs project, not Google Family Link. It does not manage a child’s Google account or control their phone.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>',image=image)
 page('/nearcrew/privacy/','NearCrew Offline Chat Privacy Policy','Local chat, photos, voice, optional locations, permissions and deletion in NearCrew Offline Chat.',STYLE+'''<article class="fl"><h1>Your nearby chat.<br>Your choices.</h1><p>Updated November 6, 2026. Publisher: TripperDeeLabs. Package: <code>com.familylink.offlinechat</code>. This policy describes the current development build, not a claim of production approval.</p><h2>No developer-operated chat server</h2><p>NearCrew connects nearby devices using Bluetooth or a local Wi-Fi hotspot. The INTERNET permission allows local sockets. The app has no cloud chat account, ads, analytics SDK, subscription or in-app purchase integration. The planned paid download is handled by Google Play; NearCrew does not receive payment-card details.</p><h2>What you share</h2><p>You choose a name and color. Confirmed room members can exchange text, small photos, voice notes, call audio, group alerts and meeting details. The host approves participants, relays messages and can read room content. Recipients may keep copies or screenshots. Names and colors do not prove who is holding a device.</p><p>Native Wi-Fi uses pinned TLS certificates; Bluetooth relies on Android pairing and link security. Optional browser guests use unencrypted local HTTP. Network observers may read it and active attackers may alter the page or traffic. Host approval is an admission control, not end-to-end group encryption.</p><h2>Optional location sharing</h2><p>A one-time location is shown with age and accuracy for confirmation before sending. Separately, users may enable 30- or 60-minute location sharing, with updates about every five minutes to the host and approved native-app users, including later joiners. Browser guests are excluded from timed updates. Sharing can continue with the screen locked, pauses while disconnected, and stops on expiry, leaving or app restart. Stop controls are available in the app and notification. No ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION permission is declared; user-started foreground-service location is used.</p><p>Timed positions are not stored as movement history. Recipients may retain earlier positions until expiry or keep their own copies. A one-time location sent as a message can remain in saved chat. Opening a Maps link passes coordinates to the chosen external map app or website under its own policy.</p><h2>Local storage and deletion</h2><p>Recent chat and reconnection information are stored in private, Android Keystore-backed AES-256-GCM storage. Limits are 80 entries, 10 photos, 10 voice notes and 10 queued messages. Starting or joining another room replaces that local conversation. The app does not promise unlimited retention. Saved data is accessible to someone who can unlock the phone and open the app.</p><p>While disconnected, use Saved conversation → Delete Saved Messages and Reconnection Key. Deletion affects this device, not other participants’ copies. Clearing app storage or uninstalling also removes local data; no cloud restore is provided. Android app-data backup is disabled.</p><h2>Permissions</h2><p>Nearby devices and Bluetooth permissions support local discovery, pairing and connections. Nearby Wi-Fi and network permissions support the hotspot. Older Android discovery may require location permission. Camera access supports QR scanning and flashlight signaling; photo selection uses Android’s picker. Microphone access supports user-started voice calls and recordings. Voice-call audio is not intentionally saved as a recording by the app; voice notes are stored when sent. Unsent note drafts are discarded when leaving the app.</p><p>Notifications show active chat and sharing status and incoming room alerts. Foreground-service types are connectedDevice, microphone and location, used for their respective active tasks. Location sharing and voice use are optional. The app does not request contacts, phone-call management, SMS or advertising-ID permission.</p><h2>Feedback and installer sharing</h2><p>Feedback opens your email app with a draft to tripperdeelabs@gmail.com; you decide whether to send. Optional diagnostics can be previewed and include only app version, Android API, layout, text size, theme, connection type and room state. They exclude names, messages, device identifiers, PINs, locations, network addresses and logs. Your own text and email address can still contain personal information. Contact support to request deletion of correspondence.</p><p>Installer sharing exposes only a copied app APK through a temporary read grant. It does not export chat history. Split-package installations cannot be shared as one complete installer. Review links remain hidden until a verified store listing is configured.</p><h2>Adult audience and launch status</h2><p>NearCrew is intended for adults aged 18 and older. Native users confirm locally before chat is available; the app saves a confirmation boolean on that device. Browser users make the choice before joining or resuming on each page load. No birth date or identity document is collected. This is self-declaration, not verified age. This is a development preview; privacy and social-app safety requirements remain under review. There is no open public chat directory or stranger-matching feature. An adult declaration, room PIN or host approval does not verify identity or guarantee safe content.</p><h2>This website and contact</h2><p>Website hosting and optional analytics are separate from the app. See the <a href="/privacy/">website privacy policy</a>. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>',image=image)
 page('/nearcrew/support/','NearCrew Offline Chat Support','Help joining a nearby room, browser invitations, permissions, saved chat and optional location sharing.',STYLE+'''<article class="fl"><h1>A little help<br>getting connected.</h1><h2>Start with one host</h2><p>Set your profile name and color. One Android phone chooses Create a room, then Bluetooth or Wi-Fi hotspot. Everyone stays nearby and uses the same connection type. Up to six participants can share the room, including the host. Keep the host powered on.</p><h2>Join with the Android app</h2><p>Choose Join someone nearby. For Bluetooth, enter the six-digit room PIN, find the host and follow Android pairing prompts. For Wi-Fi, use the host’s app-room QR invitation. Wait for the host to approve you. Do not share invitation codes publicly.</p><h2>Join in a browser</h2><p>The Wi-Fi host selects Help someone join → No app / iPhone. Scan the Wi-Fi QR first, then the Open chat QR. These are separate steps. Enter your name and wait for approval. Keep the webpage open. Automatic hotel-style captive-portal opening is not implemented. Browser chat is text-only and unencrypted; iPhone/Safari behavior still needs release qualification.</p><h2>Delivery and reconnecting</h2><p>Local only means nobody else received the message. Received by host does not mean every person received or read it. Check the connection indicator, move closer and use Reconnect or Retry. A restarted hotspot may require a fresh invitation. VPN or manufacturer battery settings can interfere with local networking. NearCrew does not relay across town or through other group members.</p><h2>Photos, voice and meetings</h2><p>Use the plus control for attachments. Voice notes are limited to 30 seconds; preview before sending. Tap your own confirmed text to edit it. The host can pin a meeting plan, which participants acknowledge; an edited plan needs a new acknowledgment. Browser guests cannot use native photos or voice features. Real multi-device photo, call and recording acceptance remains part of preview testing.</p><h2>Locations are optional</h2><p>Preview a one-time location before sending, or open Group locations and choose a timed sharing duration. Android location permission and notifications are needed for timed sharing. Confirm Start sharing separately. Stop from the app or notification. Maps displays a snapshot and may need downloaded maps or internet access. Positions can become stale; they do not prove someone is safe.</p><h2>Read or delete saved chat</h2><p>Saved conversation shows this phone’s bounded recent history. Delete saved messages and reconnection information while disconnected. Other participants keep their own copies. Starting or joining another room replaces the saved conversation. There is no chat export or unlimited archive.</p><h2>Appearance and accessibility</h2><p>Choose Light, Dark or Follow system in Appearance. Adjust chat text size or use Simple mode. Home icons return to the main screen; room controls explicitly distinguish navigating from leaving a connection.</p><h2>Price and availability</h2><p>Planned $0.99 US one-time paid download, with no ads or subscriptions. The app is not yet on Google Play. Child-audience controls and device qualification must be completed before public launch. This is not an emergency communication or remote child-monitoring service.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Use Provide feedback for a previewable email draft, or email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>. Include app version, Android version and a non-sensitive description. Do not send chat histories, PINs, invitation codes or exact locations.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>',image=image)
